  "operative_text": "Sec. 5d(1) (amending MCL 28.425d): Sec. 5d. {+(1) If the county clerk issues a notice of statutory disqualification because of an error on the application by the applicant, the applicant may submit a new application under section 5b or 5+}{+l+}{+ with the corrected information within 21 business days after receiving the notice of statutory disqualification without paying an additional fee. If an applicant determines that the applicant made an error on the application before receiving a notice of statutory disqualification from a county clerk, the applicant may submit an updated application within 21 business days after submitting the original application under section 5b or 5+}{+l+}{+ without paying an additional fee. If a county clerk issues a notice of statutory disqualification because of an error by an individual other than the applicant, the applicant may submit a new application under section 5b or 5+}{+l+}{+ at any time without paying an additional fee if the applicant submits supporting documents that correct the error.+}"
}